      "summary": ": Monday 27 July 2026 Another beauty to kick off the week! Clear skies, calm winds and cold temps are back on the menu, and the mountain is looking absolutely mint for it. Recent fresh snowfall combined with those continuing cool temps has the snowpack sitting in fantastic condition — soft, settled and ready to shred. Our grooming crew were out overnight laying down corduroy, and with snowmaking conditions perfect, they've been hard at it building up the Home Basin. Add it all up and you've got an epic day on tap right across the mountain, top to bottom. Blue skies will dominate for most of the day, with some high cloud sneaking in late in the arvo. Banger of a Monday, get on up here and make the most of it! See you on the hill!",
